## What was built

Split the site into independent first-wave tasks by file ownership: HTML structure, CSS, frontend JavaScript, shared content data, and backend server/package work can proceed in parallel because each edits distinct files. Tests depend on the backend contract, and the final integration task depends on all implementation tasks so it can wire references, resolve merge issues, verify the browser/server flow, and update documentation without parallel file conflicts.


